<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP Dec steel output inches higher.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP Dec steel output inches higher.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's biggest raw steel maker, The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP), on Monday reported its December steel production had inched higher in December, but lower exports saw despatches slip five percent during the month.</p>
<p>&quot;Internationally, steel markets remain very competitive with excess supply and price pressures,&quot; BHP said in its monthly production report.</p>
<p>Commissioning in December of steelmaking and slab casting facilities at the North Star BHP joint venture in Delta, Ohio, contributed 659 tonnes to total steelmake, BHP said.  </p>
<p>The company said Australian domestic despatches for December were 12 percent higher than a year ago but exports slid 21.5 percent due mainly to shipment timings.</p>
<p>Despatches from other overseas operations reflect the contribution of new metallic coating capacity in the United States.  </p>
